+This node owns visit persistence and the meaning of a current visit when independently edited copies arrive. A visit is identified by a client-generated UUID and refers to a catalog plot UUID. Updates can arrive days after their starting state was fetched, because a tablet may be offline for 48 hours. The server must not treat arrival order as evidence that one worker's observations are more authoritative.
 
